.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-SESSION 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-session
.Nd open a terminal in the browser onto a shell, a VM console or a pod, behind the web console's address
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm open
.Ar kind
.Ar target
.Op Fl -user Ar name
.Op Fl -title Ar text
.Nm
.Cm close
.Ar id
.Nm
.Cm list | prune
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Everything in the web console that needs a window onto something \(em a
virtual machine's serial console, a shell in a pod, an ssh session to a
cluster node, a klab run's log \(em opens it through
.Nm .
.Cm open
starts
.Pa kldload-session@ Ns Ar id Ns Pa .service ,
a
.Xr ttyd 1
running the command on a unix socket only the web server's group can
open, adds a location
.Pa /s/ Ns Ar id Ns Pa /
to the web server on port 8443, reloads it, and prints the address.
.Ar id
is eight random hexadecimal digits.
Every open and close is logged.
.Pp
The kinds:
.Bl -tag -width "vm-serial" -compact
.It Cm shell
.Ar target
is the command, or
.Ql -
for a login shell.
.It Cm vm-serial
The serial console of the libvirt domain
.Ar target .
.It Cm vm-ssh
ssh to the address or host name
.Ar target ,
as root and then as admin.
.It Cm pod-exec
A shell in
.Ar namespace Ns / Ns Ar pod Ns Op / Ns Ar container .
.It Cm node-ssh
ssh to the host
.Ar target
as root.
.It Cm klab-tail
.Ql klab tail Ar target .
.El
.Pp
Every target but a shell command must match a plain pattern of letters,
digits and a few punctuation marks, or it is refused before anything is
started.
It must run as root.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm open Ar kind Ar target
As above.
.Fl -user
names who asked, for the log;
.Fl -title
is shown in the browser tab.
.It Cm close Ar id
Stop the session, remove its location and reload the web server.
.It Cm list
The sessions open.
.It Cm prune
Close every session whose service has ended.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/lib/kldload/sessions/ Ns Ar id Ns Pa .env
The session's record, mode 0640; read back as shell, so every value is
written quoted with
.Ql printf %q .
.It Pa /etc/nginx/conf.d/kldload-dyn/ Ns Ar id Ns Pa .conf
Its location in the web server.
.It Pa /run/kldload/session/ Ns Ar id Ns Pa .sock
Its terminal, mode 0660, group the web server's.
.It Pa /var/log/kldload-session.log
Every open and close.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when done; 1 on a refusal or a failure, named.
.Sh EXAMPLES
On a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-session list
(no active sessions)
# (exited 0)
# kldload-session open vm-serial 'bad;name'
[kldload-session] error: invalid VM name: bad;name
# (exited 1)
# kldload-session open vm-ssh '1.2.3.4;id'
[kldload-session] error: invalid vm-ssh target: 1.2.3.4;id (expected IP or hostname)
# (exited 1)
# kldload-session open pod-exec 'NS/pod;x'
[kldload-session] error: pod-exec target must be <namespace>/<pod>[/<container>]
# (exited 1)
# kldload-session open frob x
[kldload-session] error: unsupported kind: frob (supported: shell vm-serial vm-ssh pod-exec node-ssh klab-tail)
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Pp
Opening one; not run for this page, since it puts a root console on the
network:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-session open vm-serial web01
# prints https://<host>:8443/s/<id>/
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ttyd 1 ,
.Xr kldload-webui 8 ,
.Xr nginx 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-30, writing this page:
.Cm pod-exec
never named the pod \(em a shell quirk emptied it \(em so no pod shell
ever opened; and the session record was written with only the command
quoted, so a quote in a title would have run as root when the record was
next read.
Until the same day a session's terminal listened on a loopback port, and
its address was all that guarded it; it now needs the console's sign-in.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
The web server serves
.Pa /s/ Ns Ar id Ns Pa /
only to a browser signed in to the console (see
.Xr kldload-webui 8 ) ,
and the consoles run as root: anyone who can sign in has them.
Sessions do not expire when idle, and
.Cm prune
closes only those whose service has already ended.
A session opened before 2026-09-30 has no socket in its record and will
not start again; close it and open a new one.
